### `reference-harness/fixtures/*/deck/files/` — the compiled bundles inside the fixture decks

The two committed reference-harness fixture decks each carry the deck's own
compiled asset outputs as their card content, under file ids `307` (the
`*all+*script` output, `.js`) and `447` (the `*all+*style` output, `.css`):

- `reference-harness/fixtures/synthetic-v1/deck/files/307/*.js`
- `reference-harness/fixtures/synthetic-v1/deck/files/447/*.css`
- `reference-harness/fixtures/write-battery-v1/deck/files/307/*.js`
- `reference-harness/fixtures/write-battery-v1/deck/files/447/*.css`

**Why compiled outputs ship inside a fixture deck:** these files are the
fixture decks' own committed card content, not build inputs. Decko stores a
deck's compiled `*all+*script` and `*all+*style` outputs as File cards, and the
reference harness drives a real Decko schema — a fixture whose deck were
missing its asset outputs would not be the deck the oracle answered against.
They are consequently subject to the same notice-destroying concatenation
problem as the demo bundles above, which is why they are listed here. The
licenses are the ones already shipped in the `fixtures/vendor/` inventory
above, unmodified and in the same terms; `PROVENANCE.md` beside the demo
bundles maps section markers to those same files.

