### The one that constrains redistribution

**TinyMCE is LGPL-2.1.** Every other component above is MIT or Apache-2.0,
which require only that the notice travel with the software. LGPL-2.1
requires more: a redistributor must also make the library's source available
(section 6), which this project satisfies — it is GPL-3.0-or-later, and the
GPL's section 6 is the same copy-and-modify mechanism. TinyMCE is also
available from Tiny under a commercial license; choosing that arm is a
licensing decision for whoever redistributes the package, not a code change,
because the vendored bytes are identical either way.

